      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what fails first, and drop \"native\", since the bug isn\u0027t specific to P3S? Something like:\n\n```\nASHMEM_GET_PIN_STATUS is defined with _IO(), so _IOC_SIZE() is zero\nfor it, and the reader that ioctl() builds from it can\u0027t hold a struct\nashmem_pin. The ioctl then always fails with -EFAULT.\n\nRead sizeof(struct ashmem_pin) for all three pin ioctls, as the C\ndriver did.\n```\n\nCould you also add `Fixes: 88767401147c (\"ANDROID: ashmem_rust: add ASHMEM_PIN/UNPIN\")` after `Bug:`, as 0e168fbe93ac (\"ANDROID: ashmem: fix integer underflow on len\u003d\u003d0\") does?",
      "isAi": true,
