      "message": "Nit: rustfmt formats this arm as `\u003d\u003e me.pin_unpin(...)`, which is why aosp/4367960 reformats it. Would a local `size` keep the existing `pin_unpin()` line and stay rustfmt-clean? Something like:\n\n```\n            ASHMEM_PIN | ASHMEM_UNPIN | ASHMEM_GET_PIN_STATUS \u003d\u003e {\n                // ASHMEM_GET_PIN_STATUS is _IO(), so _IOC_SIZE(cmd) is 0.\n                let size \u003d core::mem::size_of::\u003cbindings::ashmem_pin\u003e();\n                me.pin_unpin(cmd, UserSlice::new(UserPtr::from_addr(arg), size).reader())\n            }\n```\n\nThen aosp/4367960 wouldn\u0027t need to touch this arm.",
